>	1. blessed tinning kit [I really like having one of these; nothing hurts more than munching a dragon then finding a tengu and killing him and having to 
>watch the corpse rot; also makes meals such as dragons much less filling which
>is actually good at times]

I agree on this one, if you don't find a tinning kit through other
means. Lots of advantages to having one:

* Stock up on tins of floating eye meat, in case you lose telepathy.
  Similarly, tin all the Quantum Mechanics you find, so you can speed
  up if a shade takes away your intrinsic speed. Hell, until you
  genocide gremlins, you'll want to keep a few tins for each
  intrinsic.

* Tin all those giant zombies & mummies, getting untainted tins of
  giant meat. Nice way to max out STR.

* Tin all those big, heavy, intrinsic granting monsters (dragons,
  fire/frost giants, etc.) before eating them.

* Reverse genocide tengus, then tin them as you kill them. Makes it
  much more likely you'll gain TC, since one corpse won't rot while
  you're eating another.

>	Though just occurred to me.  Can you wish for a living critter?  Like,
>a gray dragon?  Not a particularly useful ability, but just curious.

I don't believe so, but you *can* wish for figurines or cursed scrolls
of genocide, which do the job nicely.
